# The names Kiali's copy of Tempo's query IDL declares, one per line, as
# "Service/Rpc" or "Message.field". hack/gen-tempo-protos.sh keeps these and
# nothing else, taking every field number from upstream.
#
# Names, never numbers: a rename is what breaks a reader of upstream's IDL, and
# a name that has gone makes the generator stop. The numbers are upstream's, and
# the generator asserts each name still carries the same one in every release in
# TEMPO_VERSIONS.

StreamingQuerier/Search

SearchRequest.Tags
SearchRequest.MinDurationMs
SearchRequest.Limit
SearchRequest.start
SearchRequest.end
SearchRequest.Query
SearchRequest.SpansPerSpanSet

SearchResponse.traces
SearchResponse.metrics

TraceSearchMetadata.traceID
TraceSearchMetadata.rootServiceName
TraceSearchMetadata.rootTraceName
TraceSearchMetadata.startTimeUnixNano
TraceSearchMetadata.durationMs
TraceSearchMetadata.spanSet
TraceSearchMetadata.spanSets

SpanSet.spans
SpanSet.matched
SpanSet.attributes

Span.spanID
Span.name
Span.startTimeUnixNano
Span.durationNanos
Span.attributes

SearchMetrics.inspectedTraces
SearchMetrics.inspectedBytes
SearchMetrics.totalBlocks
SearchMetrics.completedJobs
SearchMetrics.totalJobs
SearchMetrics.totalBlockBytes
